  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chronic Crisis Case for Support People on the Move Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the Africa region, the Global Route Based Migration Programme will be in implemented by 15 National Societies in West and Central Africa, East Africa, and the Sahel regions (Benin, Burkina Faso, Cameroon, Chad, Cote d&apos;Ivoire, Ethiopia, the Gambia, Ghana, Mali, Mauritania, Niger, Nigeria, Senegal, Sudan, and Togo). The programme is designed to be scaled up and extended as routes and needs evolve.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Migration Case for Support is IFRC&apos;s Global Route Based Migration Programme. Every day, people make the decision to undertake dangerous and arduous journeys in search of safety or better opportunities. During their travel, migrants, refugees, asylum seekers and other displaced people face extraordinary challenges. Their lives, dignity and human rights are at risk and they are often confronted with constrained access to food and water, shelter, information, healthcare and communication.</narrative>
  </description>
